  "note": "2010-2024 sourced from exchange_calendars only (backfill; not independently verified). 2025-2027: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications (Euronext's holiday calendar, published to 2027). 2028-2029: predicted from exchange_calendars and Euronext's unchanged holiday pattern; Euronext has not published those years, although the entries cite its calendar page. regular_hours: close 17:30 before 2012-08-06, 16:30 after. Oslo Børs cut trading hours by one hour on 2012-08-06; 16:30 includes the closing auction (continuous trading ends 16:20, which is the single close exchange_calendars has for 2000-2026, so its pre-2012-08-06 hours are wrong). The 17:30 close before the cut is inferred from the one-hour reduction and is dated from the start of the registry, not from a notice. Rechecked 2026-11-19 (4c-R2) against Euronext's trading-hours-and-holidays page. Fixed: the Wednesday before Easter is an Oslo half trading day every year (Euronext lists 2025-04-16, 2026-04-01 and 2027-03-24 as half trading days for Oslo only); exchange_calendars and the 2011-2024 backfill had it, but 2025-2029 did not. Added the three published dates and an easter_offset -4 early_close rule (effective_from 2025-01-01) that also generates 2028-04-12 and 2029-03-28. Half-day time 13:00 is the end of continuous trading, as in exchange_calendars and the 2011-2024 entries; Euronext's 2024 half-day schedule has a closing call 13:00-13:05 and Trading At Last to 13:10 (closed 13:10), so 13:00 is earlier than the 16:30 full-day convention, which includes the closing auction. The 2025-2027 schedules' times were not readable here. Dec 24/31 are full closures (rules), as Euronext lists. Hours: no change after 2012-08-06 was found (continuous 09:00-16:20, closing at 16:20 per the 2020 Optiq migration guidelines); no 2020 COVID-19 closure.",
